# Story 49: Reading & Searching Files (45s)
# Hook: Point the agent at your code -- ls, file_read, glob, and grep find anything, no approval required.
# Duration: 45s
# Source: story-049-reading-searching-files.tape
#
# Voiceover script with timing cues.
# Format: [START --> END] narration text
# Each entry should be spoken within its time window.
# Gaps between entries are silent (viewer watches the demo).
#
# Total segments: 6

[00:00.0 --> 00:03.0]
Point the agent at your code -- ls, file_read, glob, and grep find anything, no approval required.

[00:03.0 --> 00:08.0]
Start rysh in a project directory you want to explore.

[00:08.0 --> 00:14.0]
Double-press Escape to switch to prompt mode and talk to the agent.

[00:14.0 --> 00:30.0]
Ask it to find all the TODO comments. It reaches for grep with a regex, glob to walk the tree with double-star patterns, and file_read to peek inside. These are read-only tools, so they run without asking for approval.

[00:30.0 --> 00:42.0]
Behind that single request: ls for quick listings, glob for pattern matching, grep for content search, file_read for contents, and tree for structure -- the agent picks whichever fits, and shows you exactly what it found.

[00:42.0 --> 00:45.0]
Read and search the whole codebase, just by asking.

